const IFACE = (abiOld) => 'INTERFACE (fixed; every agent uses exactly this; the numbers N = ' + abiOld + ' and N+1 = ' + (abiOld + 1) + ' are the OM_ABI_VERSION the Preflight read on the merged base and the one this piece sets):\n' +
  '  C, public (csrc/ouroboros_sim.h): a hand-written typedef OUTSIDE the generated blocks, placed with the other struct typedefs next to om_lot (:1086 on 01c2e752): typedef struct om_route_point { double x; double y; int32_t layer; } om_route_point; (24 bytes on LP64: 8 + 8 + 4 + 4 pad; offsets x 0, y 8, layer 16; a comment says so and that the pad is not written meaningfully). The declaration uint32_t om_unit_route_get(const om_world *w, uint32_t id, om_route_point *buf, uint32_t cap, int *reachable); (five parameters, Architect round 3 g1 (A)) is GENERATED by scripts/specfactory/sig_table.py --emit from ONE new row of docs/northstar/spec_factory/signatures.toml: name om_unit_route_get, module tactical_move.c, restype uint32_t, params w const om_world*, id uint32_t, buf om_route_point *, cap uint32_t, reachable int *, epics ["E-13"], confidence "likely", a note that states the semantics below. [ONE row, five parameters; the g1 ruling wins over the four-parameter first ruling.] OM_ABI_VERSION N to N+1 in the header (with its comment), signatures.toml [meta] abi_version, tests/csim/conftest.py EXPECTED_ABI_VERSION.\n' +
  '  Semantics of om_unit_route_get (body in csrc/tactical_move.c next to om_move_route_get, which it wraps; it may use the static helpers of that file): returns the number of points of the unit\'s planned walking route and writes min(count, cap) points to buf when buf is not NULL (buf NULL or cap 0 writes nothing; the return is the FULL count even when cap is smaller, as om_move_route_get does); 0 for an unknown id, a unit with no movement row, a world with no movement state, and a unit with no stored route (g3). *reachable is written on EVERY path when the pointer is not NULL: with a stored route 1 iff route_ends_at_goal (read from the movement row through om_move_get, as om_move_route_get reads the row; om_move_route_get keeps its prototype and the W2 tests stay unedited), else 0; with no stored route 1 for every unit (a world with no movement state, an unknown id, a unit with no movement row, no order, an arrived walker, a plan over 512 points, the slope-crossing drop, a plan of fewer than 2 points, a flyer; walker or not, destination or not; g3 audit version). Slot 0 is the unit\'s current position (x, y of the movement row); the following points are the stored route\'s points rebuilt by W2\'s expression from route_i on (g2 (a)), so count = 1 + route_n - route_i. Layer: slot 0 carries the unit layer (om_move_layer), every other point om_terrain_band_at(w, x, y) - 1 (g4 (b)); band 0 (no terrain, or an unbanded cell) -> the unit\'s layer. It reads through om_move_get only, never om_move_touch: a call changes no checksum, no save byte and no row. No allocation, no state.\n' +
  '  Pipe verb (csrc/pipe/om_pipe.c): request {"type":"cmd","name":"unit_route","id":<unit id>}; answer ONE frame {"type":"route","id":<id>,"points":[[x,y,layer],...],"reachable":true|false} with x, y written by jb_double (wu, the coordinates of the tactical frame\'s units) and layer by jb_int, points in accessor order, at most 512 points (about 20 KB); reachable = the accessor *reachable as a JSON bool (jb_bool); errors {"type":"error","name":"unit_route","reason":...} with the reasons "no world" (W NULL), "not begun" (in_recon(), the command verb gate), "missing field" (id absent or not an unsigned 32 bit integer) and "no unit" (om_unit_alive false: an unknown or dead id), all per g3. The handler is static void handle_unit_route(const char *json) placed after handle_space_field_dump, called from the dispatch chain right after the space_field_dump line [G5]; it calls PUBLIC symbols only; it writes no tactical frame and no ack. The frame size is RECORDED by the transport test, not bounded (no number was given). The verb is read-only: no checksum change, not a command, not logged.\n' +
  '  Docs: docs/architecture.md gets ONE paragraph "VG-CONTRACT-route (2026-10-14, the planned route reaches the client)" in the style of the K-e5 and VG-W2 paragraphs (the typedef and its layout, the accessor and its semantics, the verb and its frame and errors, reachable, the points rule, the layer rule, the 512 bound, read-only, ABI N to N+1, no save or checksum change, the customer VG-A-routeline, See also the W2 paragraph and the tests), a bullet for unit_route beside the space_field_dump and terrain_probe bullets, the hello example abi and the abi history line.'

const ruler = (r) => agent(RULES + '\nRole: ruler (Engineer), rules.md section (e). Builder branch origin/' + r.branch + ' stopped with: ' + r.stop_reason + '\nSpec: ' + SPEC + '. Rulebook: docs/northstar/plans/2026-10-07-visible-game-rulebook.md (its "Decision procedure" word for word; lane E rows are TD-VG-E-<n> in docs/northstar/plans/push_ledger_2026-09-22.md, next free number after the highest present). Branch push/vg-croute-rulings (suffix vg-croute-rulings; continue it from origin if it exists: worktree add ~/Projects/om-push/wt/vg-croute-rulings origin/push/vg-croute-rulings then git checkout -B push/vg-croute-rulings, else from ' + BASE + '). If every condition of the procedure holds: edit only the one test file named, run it alone and its positive control, append the ledger row, push, report ruled true with row and branch. Else report ruled false and brief (under one page: test id and failing line, the builder\'s claim, the ruling and gap lines that bear on it, two or three options with what each changes). A threshold, window or tolerance is never ruled. A test-defect that encodes the answer to a GAP (1 to 4) is ruled false (the Architect rules gaps).', { label: 'rule:' + r.branch, phase: 'Build', schema: RULING, agentType: 'engineer', model: 'sonnet' })
const withRuling = async (mk) => {
  let r = await mk('')
  if (r && !r.ok && /^test-defect:/.test(r.stop_reason || '')) {
    const v = await ruler(r)
    if (v && v.ruled && v.branch) { r = await mk(', origin/' + v.branch + ' (ruling ' + v.row + ')'); r = { ...r, ruling: v } } else { r = { ...r, ruling: v } }
  }
  return r
}

